<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells tin in long-term contract.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells tin in long-term contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 5,000 tonnes of surplus longhorn tin to Considar Inc of New York at a provisional fair market value in excess of $31 million.</p>
<p>The agency gave no further details of the long-term contract.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
